### 1.1. How to get the source code

The complete corresponding source is in this same repository:

* `qemu/patches/` — every patch we apply to QEMU;
* `qemu/src/` — our own files, compiled into QEMU;
* `qemu/build-android.sh` — the build script (it also downloads the upstream
  QEMU tarball and applies the patches). The build is pinned: the script checks
  the sha256 of the QEMU archive and of the Alpine root it builds in, and writes
  `qemu/build/BUILD-MANIFEST.txt` (package versions, compiler, patches, checksum
  of the result). See `README.md`.

To rebuild `libqemu.so` from source, on an **aarch64 Linux** host with root:

```bash
sudo ./qemu/build-android.sh
```

