## 2. Libraries bundled inside the application package

### 2.1. Bouncy Castle 1.70 — Bouncy Castle Licence

`bcprov`, `bctls`, `bcpkix` and `bcutil` (version 1.70) are bundled **inside**
the application package.

Why they are there: the guest system speaks only TLS 1.0, which current Android
no longer offers — its TLS provider dropped TLSv1 entirely. So our proxy speaks
TLS to the guest itself, in pure Java, and uses the phone’s modern TLS when
talking to the outside world.

* licence text: `licenses/BouncyCastle.txt` (reproduced verbatim from
  `org/bouncycastle/LICENSE` inside the distributed jar);
* source code: `https://github.com/bcgit/bc-java` (tag `r1rv70`).

The jars are used **unmodified**.

### 2.2. Kotlin standard library 2.0.21 and JetBrains annotations 13.0 — Apache License 2.0

The application is written in Kotlin. The Kotlin standard library (the `kotlin`
packages, about a thousand classes and its `.kotlin_builtins` resources) and the
