## 5. Guest firmware and anything installed inside it

⚠️ **Not part of this package and not licensed here.**

This application ships **no firmware at all**. The user supplies their own
archive, and the application unpacks it on the device. Any firmware, and any
application inside it, belongs to its own rights holder.

Neither this repository nor the application provides links to download any
firmware.

You are responsible for having the right to use the firmware you supply, and to
have a modified copy of it made on your own device. The application changes that
copy (patched code, re-signed packages, removed vendor modules); nothing is sent
anywhere. Package signatures of the copy are replaced with a key generated on
your device.

The application also runs a local TLS proxy: a root certificate generated on
your device is added to the trust store of the copy, so that the firmware (which
speaks only TLS 1.0) can reach the modern internet. The key never leaves the
device.

