## 6. Artwork

The artwork in this application is either **drawn by its own code** or
supplied by the project owner, and the package ships no photograph:

* there is no handset frame: the guest screen is shown on its own, and under it
  sits a key panel drawn by the application's code (`KeyPanel.kt`, package
  `tech.istratii.senses.art`, laid out and painted by `Skin.kt`) — a plain
  black strip with a "back" arrow and a "home" house outline drawn as strokes
  and, between them, the lettering described in the next item. The two key
  shapes are generic and are not taken from any other product; no image file
  is involved;
* the lettering between the on-screen keys ("SENSES"), the lettering in the
  "about" window that opens when the phone is shaken while no system is
  running ("ISTRATII_TECH"), and the launcher icon are vector drawings
  supplied by the project owner: `art/logo_menu.svg`, `art/logo_about.svg`
  and `art/icon.svg`. `tools/mkicon.py` reads the numbers from the drawings
  and renders the letters, on the maintainer's computer, into coverage masks
  (`res/drawable-nodpi/logo_menu_mask.png`, `logo_about_mask.png`) and into
  the adaptive-icon layers (`res/mipmap-*/senses_fg.png`, and the white
  themed-icon layer `senses_mono.png`); the colour
  gradient and its animation are drawn on the device (`ShineLogo.kt`). The
  drawings name a system typeface (`font-family`); the letters were
  rasterised from the copy installed on the maintainer's computer, and **no
  font file is stored in the repository or shipped in the package**. If the
  mask fails to load, plain "SENSES" in the system typeface is drawn in its
  place. The drawings carry no editor metadata.

Earlier versions of this project surrounded the guest screen with a drawing of
a handset, and before that with a photograph of one (the launcher icon was
also made from it). All of that has been removed; none of it is in the tree or
in the package.

An interim launcher icon (and the plate between the keys) was cut from an
AI-generated raster image; it was replaced by the owner's drawings above and
its file (`art/icon.jpg`) is no longer in the tree.

